# Jungle backdrop colour fidelity

Approved working state (Jul 2026): Blender materials/atlas/vertex colours reach the game unchanged. Do not reintroduce candy remaps on the dressed backdrop.

## Runtime (must keep)

- `scene.glb` loads with `preserveMaterials: true` — **no** `MeshToon` / palette / foliageFlat / green multiply.
- Arena prop GLBs (`tree`, `stump`, `fern`, `vine`, `piranha`) stay on the separate candy toon path.
- Do not call `tintByMaterialName` / day-night palette on backdrop mats (`PixelPalette*`, `Material*`, `MAT_GroundMix`).
- Cache-bust `scene.glb` (`?v=gfxN`) after every re-export.
- Split preload in `themes/index.js`: backdrop ≠ props.

## Export (must keep)

Canonical script: `art/jungle/scripts/fix_blender_fidelity_export.py`

- Restore **original** NatureKit `Texture.png` — never brighten/gamma-hack the atlas.
- Bake `PixelPalette_JungleMid/Warm/Dark` HueSat into separate textures (glTF drops HueSat nodes).
- Bake ground `Col` mask → `ColBake` display RGB; export **only** `ColBake` as COLOR_0 (stash `Col`, restore after). Multiple colour layers → grey ground.
- Palms: Principled `Material.001` (trunk) + `Material.002` (fronds); both face slots required.
- Before export: uniquify linked VEG meshes **without** `materials.clear()` (clear resets face `material_index` → palms lose leaves; shared meshes → all bushes become one PixelPalette).

## Forbidden regressions

- Stripping glTF maps with a restrictive `maps={}` on the backdrop.
- Forcing flat greens on `VEG_Bush` / reeds / rocks.
- RGB boost on `PixelPalette` (salad rocks).
- Remapping `Material.001` / `Material.002` / rocks to candy palette.
- Green `hemiGround` strong enough to tint grey atlas rocks lime.
- Touching arena `surface.tileMap*` / prop toon path when fixing backdrop colours.

## Lighting polish (allowed)

Soft shadows / fill / AO / godrays in `environment.js` + `theme.shadows` / `theme.gfx` are OK.
Do **not** recolour backdrop albedos to “fix” lighting — only lights, shadows, and post.

## Quick check after changes

- Rocks sample grey atlas (not lime).
- Bushes keep Mid/Warm/Dark variants in GLB.
- Each `VEG_Palm_*` has trunk + frond materials.
- Ground shows grass / sand / basin (not flat grey).
